est records were bounded verification; and the reboot was required by the provider-wide evidence protocol. The temporary staging file and transient reboot unit were removed. After reboot there were no failed units, unexpected listeners, damaged package state, or executor staging residue; lifecycle differences were limited to the expected boot identity, process IDs, and systemd private directories.","evidence_ids":["cmd-710f01e4fb2a4628","cmd-d737ed5e9bd14caa","cmd-1d2cb8f0a9cf4801","cmd-5f851df0b3be47a0","cmd-3c7b6e0b999a4405","cmd-34037dd598c84101","cmd-363f75d874ee428d","cmd-11741c971b284e56","global:before_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The independent node-restart protocol is also complete: node1 had a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged the restart, became temporarily unavailable, returned with a different boot identity, and recovered its services, policy, preserved log data, platform, and access. Fixed lifecycle observations independently confirm the boot change and healthy final state.","limitations":["The universal claim that every sudo-executed command is recorded is supported by a global Defaults policy and representative root-to-root and root-to-nobody tests, rather than an exhaustive test of every possible identity and sudo policy path.","Log exclusion was directly tested with unique markers against the journal, /var/log/messages, and /var/log/secure; no evidence inventories every conceivable external or custom log sink."]}
